{"obsah":"<p>4 exhibitions in one day is a lot even for us, especially in just two teams. Michal Budský and Marek Tryner took a trip to far-off Pržno, where they enjoyed the local festival in front of a great audience.</p>\n\n<p><br>Martin Šimůnek and Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček with his complete kids' line-up headed Prague – Sokolov – Karlovy Vary. First up was Pražské služby, where together with the guys from Flow parkour they rode an exhibition in front of loads of spectators, who weren't put off even by the 29-degree scorcher. </p>\n\n<p>Next was the Czech Masters Road Cycling Championship organised by Cyklokili, with the awards ceremony on Sokolov square. A beautifully organised event, limited only by road closures on the course due to reconstruction work. And of course, who's a better spectator than a cyclist 🙂. </p>\n\n<p>Last up was Otovice near Karlovy Vary. A really polished village, where the locals put on a great event full of performances and rock music. We could barely drag the obstacles out of the trailer by then, but we got fired up and the spectators were incredible. We couldn't deprive them of crashes either – this time, unusually, it was Martin Šimůnek who took care of that. In the heat of battle he even flew onto his backside from over a metre and sat on the wireless microphone :) Even a world champion falls during a show once every 20 years. But the exhibition was successfully completed.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F06%2F240622_Sokolov_243-scaled.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F06%2F240622_Sokolov_243.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-247758\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"h